[
  {
    "claim": "The paper argues that dissimilar language alone does not necessarily indicate polarized positions, as political discussions naturally vary by socio-demographic group lexicon.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Therefore, dissimilar language alone does not necessarily indicate polarized positions.",
        "page": 4
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "The paper argues against relying on network-based approaches for measuring polarization due to restricted access to user- and network-level data under recent platform policy changes.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "However, access to user- and network-level data has become increasingly restricted, particularly under recent platform policy changes. Consequently, our study adopts a strictly text-based method, which remains both accessible and scalable for analyzing large-scale digital discourse.",
        "page": 3
      }
    ]
  }
]

[
  {
    "claim": "The study used an approximation algorithm to compute partisan polarization scores from user embeddings, validating that the method achieves high accuracy with low error when sampling around 10,000 users.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "As shown in Fig 4, the absolute error drops dramatically at around 3,000 users and falls below 0.001 at approximately 10,000 users.",
        "page": 11
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "User party affiliation was validated by matching Twitter users to official primary voter registration records in five U.S. states and Washington DC, achieving classification accuracies of 74.35% for profile-based and 73.35% for activity-based classifiers.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Our profile classifier achieved 74.35% accuracy and our activity classifier achieved 73.35% accuracy when compared to these official records.",
        "page": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Using our geolocation and voter record matching, we successfully matched over 30,000 users across these regions with their voter records",
        "page": 9
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "The analysis confirmed a strong negative correlation (r = −0.77) between regional vaccine polarization in the U.S. and actual vaccination rates one year later.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Using official CDC vaccination data from a comparable period after vaccines became available (October 11, 2021 to January 3, 2022), we confirm a strong negative correlation (r = −0.77, p < 0.001) between vaccine polarization and vaccination rates.",
        "page": 16
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "In the United States, a statistically significant negative correlation was found between the volume of conspiracy-related tweets and aggregate daily partisan polarization.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "In the United States (B), we find there is a statistically significant correlation −0.247 with CI=[−0.448,-0.023] (n = 88, p = 0.031) between these measures.",
        "page": 21
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "The study found no statistically significant correlation between the volume of conspiracy-related tweets and aggregate daily partisan polarization in Canada.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "In Canada (D), we find that there is no statistically significant correlation of 0.023 with CI=[−0.187,0.231] (n = 88, p = 0.831) between these measures.",
        "page": 21
      }
    ]
  }
]

[
  {
    "claim": "The study does not establish causality between partisan voting patterns, polarization scores, and vaccination rates, nor does it identify a single explanation for the relationship between conservative politics and higher polarization.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "While we cannot establish causality among conservative voting patterns, polarization scores, and vaccination rates, our results suggest polarized discourse played a significant role in shaping the heterogeneous vaccination landscape across the U.S.",
        "page": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "While our analysis did not identify a single explanation for the relationship between conservative politics and higher polarization, state-specific trajectories provide insights.",
        "page": 23
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "The semantic similarity approach to measuring polarization may obscure signals not captured by semantic embedding representations.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "First, we measured partisan polarization only through the proxy of semantic similarity, which may in certain cases obscure signals not captured by semantic embedding representations.",
        "page": 24
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "The classification of users into partisan groups relies on self-reported information, which may not be entirely accurate.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Additionally, our classification into partisan groups relies on self-reported information, which may not be entirely accurate.",
        "page": 24
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "Geographic attribution of users is subject to inaccuracies if users provide false, incomplete, or humorous locations, and may be affected by the use of VPNs or fake accounts.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Furthermore, the use of VPNs or fake accounts (including bots) may introduce additional error. Automated accounts can contribute disproportionately to partisan discourse by generating large volumes of ideologically slanted content or amplifying existing narratives, potentially inflating the apparent semantic distance between political groups.",
        "page": 24
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "Differences in keyword strategies between the U.S. and Canadian datasets may have contributed to cross-national differences in observed polarization patterns.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "This asymmetry may have contributed to cross-national differences in patterns of observed polarization, and this should be considered when interpreting the comparative results.",
        "page": 25
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "The temporal mismatch between the Twitter dataset collected in late 2020 and regional vaccination rates that occurred primarily in 2021 means that correlations between early discourse and later vaccination uptake are suggestive rather than causative.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Seventh, there are temporal mismatches between our Twitter dataset (collected in late 2020) and regional vaccination rates, which occurred primarily in 2021. As a result, correlations between polarization in vaccine-related discussions and later vaccination uptake should be understood as suggestive rather than causative.",
        "page": 25
      }
    ]
  }
]

[
  {
    "claim": "The paper disputes the notion that linguistic dissimilarity alone necessarily indicates polarized positions, arguing instead that it must be conditioned on specific contentious topics to reflect alternative semantic understandings.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Therefore, dissimilar language alone does not necessarily indicate polarized positions.",
        "page": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "However, when examining discussions on the same contentious topic, language dissimilarity between different partisan groups more likely reflects alternative semantic understandings of that specific topic—a phenomenon we hypothesize correlates strongly with polarization.",
        "page": 3
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "claim": "The paper builds on the finding that vaccine hesitancy is linked to political affiliation in Canada, noting that Conservative Party supporters are more likely to refuse vaccination, while also highlighting that widespread vaccine mandates may moderate the impact of online polarization.",
    "quotes": [
      {
        "text": "Like in the U.S., vaccine hesitancy was linked to political affiliation in Canada, with Conservative Party supporters more likely to refuse vaccination [96].",
        "page": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "The relatively lower influence of polarization on vaccine attitudes in Canada may be attributed to the country’s more widespread vaccine mandates [98,99].",
        "page": 24
      }
    ]
  }
]

